# Every path, one owner. The repository has a single maintainer, so this file
# exists to make review required rather than to route it: without an owner,
# GitHub's branch protection has nobody to ask.
*       @gufranco

# The three files that decide what everything else is checked against. A change
# to any of them changes what "correct" means for the whole package.
/conformance/hardware.json      @gufranco
/conformance/divergences.json   @gufranco
/conformance/suites.json        @gufranco

# What decides whether an upstream move is noticed at all. This watched one of
# two repositories for as long as it existed.
/conformance/watch.py           @gufranco
